{
  "include": ["src/**/*.ts", "src/**/*.tsx", "vite.config.ts"],
  // The 97 blocks and charts are a CATALOGUE, not application code: a site uses
  // one login layout, not five. Left in `include` they were typechecked on every
  // build whether or not anything imported them, which measured at 4.97s -> 8.02s
  // per site build. Excluded it is 5.31s.
  //
  // This does NOT weaken the check, which is the only reason it is acceptable:
  // `exclude` drops files from the INITIAL list, and TypeScript still follows an
  // import into them. Verified by breaking a chart, importing it, and confirming
  // tsc reports the error inside the excluded file — asserted in
  // test/integration/site-build.mjs so it cannot rot into a real exclusion.
  //
  // `src/components/ui` joined them 2026-07-30, when the kit reached 500. A
  // generated page imports ten or twenty; checking all 500 to cover those
  // twenty measured 8.7s against 3.2s, on every build, growing with every
  // component added.
  //
  // THE DIFFERENCE FROM THE CATALOGUE ABOVE, and why this one needed something
  // extra: the kit is code we write and change, so a component nothing happens
  // to import would stop being checked at all and the break would surface one
  // day inside a customer's build, looking like the model's fault. So the check
  // did not go away, it MOVED — `tsconfig.kit.json` typechecks all 500 and runs
  // in the test suite, once, instead of on every site build.
  //
  // `src/family-pages` WAS A THIRD ENTRY AND IS GONE WITH THE DIRECTORY.
  // Those 324 pages were the per-trade reference apps; they stopped
  // reaching the model when the families went (2026-08-20) and are now
  // test data, so they live at `test/fixtures/corpus/` instead. Out of the
  // template they cost a build nothing: `builder/Dockerfile` does
  // `COPY lovable/template/ ./`, so while they sat here they shipped 3.4 MB
  // into every build container image, excluded from this check, imported by
  // no page and typechecked by nothing at all once their own harness went.
  "exclude": ["src/components/charts", "src/components/ui"],
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2022",
    "jsx": "react-jsx",
    "module": "ESNext",
    "lib": ["ES2022", "DOM", "DOM.Iterable"],
    "types": ["vite/client"],

    /* Bundler mode */
    "moduleResolution": "Bundler",
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true,
    "verbatimModuleSyntax": false,
    "noEmit": true,

    /* Linting */
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "strict": true,
    "noUnusedLocals": false,
    "noUnusedParameters": false,
    "noFallthroughCasesInSwitch": true,
    "noUncheckedSideEffectImports": true,
    "baseUrl": ".",
    "paths": { "@/*": ["./src/*"] }
  }
}
